<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 23 February, from 1455 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1455 CE <span class="tih-ago">571 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Traditional date for the completion of the Gutenberg Bible</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition, Johannes Gutenberg's Bible was completed in Mainz around this date. It was the first major book printed in Europe with movable metal type, and print spread rapidly across the continent.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Johannes Gutenberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1685 CE <span class="tih-ago">341 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Frideric Handel is born in Halle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Handel trained in Germany and Italy before settling in London, where he wrote operas, the 'Water Music' and the oratorio 'Messiah'. He became a naturalised British subject in 1727.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1836 CE <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Siege of the Alamo begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Santa Anna's Mexican army surrounded the Texian garrison in the Alamo mission at San Antonio. After thirteen days the defenders, including Jim Bowie and Davy Crockett, were killed in the final assault.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1861 CE <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln arrives secretly in Washington</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Warned of a plot to kill him in Baltimore, President-elect Lincoln travelled through the city overnight in secret. He was mocked for the manner of his arrival, ten days before his inauguration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1905 CE <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rotary Club founded in Chicago</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lawyer Paul Harris and three business acquaintances met to found the first Rotary Club. Rotary International now has some 1.4 million members and led the campaign to eradicate polio.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Marines raise the flag on Mount Suribachi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marines planted the US flag on the summit of Iwo Jima's volcano. Joe Rosenthal's photograph of the second, larger flag won the Pulitzer Prize, though the fighting went on for another month.</p></div></li></ol>
